advice.prompt:
FlowLink task: {{mode}}.

Give the user practical advice only. Do not generate or save a replacement material unless explicitly asked in a later request. Write for a non-technical business user: plain language, concrete next actions, no selectors or technical jargon unless the user clearly has that background.

Focus on replay reliability: navigation causes, authentication redirects, target evidence, waits, state assertions, tab/system context, and data dependencies.

Recent AI-pane conversation:
{{conversation}}

User request: {{userRequest}}

Material context JSON:
{{materialContext}}
{{executionContext}}

takeover.stepTask:
{{failureContext}}

Execute exactly ONE remaining workflow step, then report.

Step {{stepIndex}} of the remaining list:
{{stepProjection}}

{{previousOutcome}}

Achieve this step's business intent in the browser. When - and only when - you can see the outcome on the page, call mark_step_done with this step index and one sentence of evidence, then finish with done=true and a one-sentence note for the user. If you cannot achieve it, finish with done=false and explain what blocked you.

takeover.retryTask:
The previous attempt at this step failed.

Step definition:
{{stepProjection}}

Attempt failure:
{{attemptError}}

Inspect the current page state first, then achieve this step's business intent with a different approach. mark_step_done still requires visible evidence; if it still cannot be done, finish with done=false.

takeover.freeRunTask:
{{previousOutcome}}

The step-by-step mode hit a step it could not complete. Switch to goal mode: complete ALL the remaining workflow steps below in order, on your own initiative, working around whatever blocked the strict attempt (popups, page changes, alternate buttons or paths) while keeping each step's business intent.

Remaining steps (the numbers are step indexes; get_step_detail(i) returns the full definition):
{{stepList}}

Work through them one by one. As soon as you can see one step's business outcome on the page, call mark_step_done with that step index and one sentence of evidence, then continue with the next. If a step is genuinely impossible, say why in a note and continue with the rest. When all are done - or the rest cannot proceed - finish with done=true and a one-sentence summary of what was achieved.
